From c444bb8bcdc16380b75c4abb1bfc37d8f5dfa9dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:15:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 135/136] dynarmic A64: B.cond as side exits, each with its own
 flags liveness

superblocks_cond: a forward B.cond whose target may be a side exit doesn't end the block:
A64ExitIfCond (a jcc to a link of its own in the cold code), the code after it translated on into
the block. Each exit gets its own flags look-ahead at its target (its live flags in the third
argument), so the dead flags pass and the selects on host flags know what the taken path reads:
with none, A64SelectOnHostFlagsPass turns the exit into A64ExitIfCondHost on the compare's own host
flags, nothing saved. The look-ahead's ranges at the exit targets go into the block's ranges for
invalidation and the persistent cache hash. game.c -7.4% instructions (24% fewer block entries).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01REmpC53sSK3VTcKMxWFSSb
